{"path":"experimental/fs/path/remove_filename","title":"std::experimental::filesystem::path::remove_filename","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::experimental::filesystem::path::</span>remove_filename","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/experimental/fs/path/remove_filename","section":"experimental","kind":"page","summary":"Removes a single filename component.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-fs_ts\" id=\"Version_1\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">path<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> remove_filename<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (1) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-fs-ts t-mark-ts\">(filesystem TS)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Removes a single filename component. \n</p><p>The behavior is undefined if the path has no filename component (<a href=\"/w/cpp/experimental/fs/path/has_path\"><code>has_filename</code></a> returns <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw2\">false</span></span></code>).\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<p>(none)\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"sy2\">*</span>this</span></code>\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Exceptions\">Exceptions</h3>\n<p>May throw implementation-defined exceptions. \n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;experimental/filesystem&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;iostream&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"kw1\">namespace</span> fs <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">experimental</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">filesystem</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> fs<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">path</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"/foo\"</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>.<span class=\"me1\">remove_filename</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span>\n              <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> fs<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">path</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"/\"</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>.<span class=\"me1\">remove_filename</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>\"/\"\n\"\"</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/experimental/fs/path/filename\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>filename</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  returns the filename path component <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/experimental/fs/path/replace_filename\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>replace_filename</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  replaces the last path component with another path <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/experimental/fs/path/has_path\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>has_filename</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  checks if the corresponding path element is not empty <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function)</span>\n</td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Exceptions","id":"Exceptions"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"experimental","title":"Experimental C++ Features"},{"path":"experimental/fs","title":"Filesystem library"},{"path":"experimental/fs/path","title":"std::experimental::filesystem::path"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::experimental::filesystem::path::remove_filename","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration. Removes a single filename component."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"(none)"},{"label":"Return value","note":"*this"},{"label":"Exceptions","note":"May throw implementation-defined exceptions."},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"filename","note":"returns the filename path component"},{"label":"replace_filename","note":"replaces the last path component with another path"},{"label":"has_filename","note":"checks if the corresponding path element is not empty"}]}]},"standards":[],"wordCount":95,"codeBlockCount":2}
